{"question_id": "V2-dev-LAW-en-T2-001", "approach": "HYBRID", "approach_base": "HYBRID", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "L", "corpus_set": "LAW_en", "answer_text": "Yes, the Act reaches this conduct, under section 6 (bribery of foreign public officials).\n\n- Section 6(1) makes it an offence for a person (\"P\") to bribe a foreign public official (\"F\") with the intention of influencing F in F's capacity as a foreign public official (evidence [4]).\n- Section 6(2) requires that P also intends to obtain or retain business or an advantage in the conduct of business — here, winning a government contract (evidence [4]).\n- Section 6(3) defines bribing: offering, promising or giving a financial or other advantage to F (directly or through a third party), where F is not permitted or required by the applicable written law to be influenced by it (evidence [4]).\n- A French ministry official is a \"foreign public official\" under section 6(5)(a), as someone holding an administrative position of a country outside the United Kingdom (evidence [6]).\n- Territorially, section 12(4)(a) gives a \"close connection\" with the UK to a British citizen, so the offence can apply even though the acts were done in France, and under section 12(3)(b) proceedings may be taken at any place in the United Kingdom (evidence [1]).", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 853 chars]", "doc_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en", "section_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::o019", "unit_ids": ["L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b167", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b168", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b169", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b170", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b171", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b172", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b173", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b174", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b175", "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b176", "L.ukpga-2010-23